// Agent protocol v1 between the Fleeto agent and fleeto-gateway.
//
// Transport:
//   CA:         HTTPS GET https://<agent host>/v1/ca returns the instance CA certificates as a PEM bundle. The agent
//               fetches it without sending anything secret, picks the CA whose SHA-256 (of the DER) equals the
//               fingerprint from the install command, and refuses to continue if none matches. (TLS stacks do not send
//               a self-signed root in the handshake, so the CA cannot be taken from the chain.)
//   Enrollment: HTTPS POST https://<agent host>/v1/enroll, body EnrollRequest, Content-Type application/x-protobuf,
//               over a connection verified normally against that CA as the only root, for the agent host name.
//               200 with EnrollResponse, or a problem+json error (400 invalid, 401 token refused, 429, 503 retry).
//   Recovery:   HTTPS POST https://<agent host>/v1/recover with the expired agent client certificate (mTLS), body
//               RecoverRequest (0.2.0). Only for a certificate that expired at most 365 days ago and was never revoked;
//               200 with RecoverResponse, or a problem+json error (401 refused, 429, 503 retry). /v1/connect answers 401
//               with the header "Fleeto-Certificate: expired" when such a certificate tries to open a session.
//   Release:    HTTPS GET https://<agent host>/v1/releases/<version>/<file> with an agent or watchdog client certificate (mTLS,
//               0.2.1): one agent binary named in the release manifest of UpdateOffer. 200 application/octet-stream, 404 when
//               the file is not part of the current release, 503 with Retry-After when too many downloads run at once.
//   Session:    WebSocket wss://<agent host>/v1/connect with the agent client certificate (mTLS).
//               Every binary WebSocket message is exactly one AgentMessage (agent to server) or ServerMessage
//               (server to agent). The WebSocket frame is the length prefix. Maximum message size 4 MiB.
//
// Signatures (ed25519, instance signing key) cover "fleeto-agent-config-v1" || 0x00 || payload, where payload
// is the exact serialized bytes carried in SignedConfig.payload. The agent never re-serializes before verifying.
// Jobs (0.2.0) use the context "fleeto-job-v1" the same way over SignedJob.payload.
//
// Watchdog (0.2.1): the second service on an endpoint connects to the same /v1/connect with its own certificate (role watchdog,
// issued through WatchdogCertificateRequest over the agent session). A watchdog session only exchanges Hello, HelloAck, Heartbeat,
// Ping, Pong, certificate renewal, UpdateOffer, UpdateStatus and Disconnect; the gateway ignores anything else it sends and never
// sends it configurations, jobs, check run or inventory requests.
//
// Updates (0.2.1): UpdateOffer carries the release manifest of the instance with its Steaan release signature (ed25519 over the
// exact manifest bytes, without a context prefix, the same signature install.sh verifies). The receiver verifies it against the
// release public keys compiled into its binary, installs only binaries named in it with the listed SHA-256 and size, and never
// a version lower than or equal to the installed one. The agent installs and updates the watchdog; the watchdog updates the agent.

